<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neuse River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Neuse River flows south-east across the coastal plain of North Carolina into Pamlico Sound. Its valley was home to Tuscarora towns and to the Neusiok people, who gave the river its name. In 1710 Swiss and German settlers founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-bern">New Bern</a> at its junction with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trento">Trent</a>, and their encroachment on Tuscarora land helped provoke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuscarora-war">Tuscarora War</a> of 1711.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neuse-river.jpg" alt="Neuse River" width="320" height="266" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Kmusser assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pamlicorivermap.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
